Error [jet.UninitializedRead]: `bytes` may be read before it is given a value
  --> tests/ui/uninit_fixed/write_argument_does_not_claim_an_uninit_buffer_was_filled.jet:5:10
    |
  5 |     noop(bytes)
    |          ^^^^^
 Why: Passing `bytes` with write access does not prove that the callee initializes it
 Fix: Write every value in `bytes` here before passing it to another function
More: jet-lang.dev/e/E0420

Error [jet.UninitializedRead]: `bytes` may be read before it is given a value
  --> tests/ui/uninit_fixed/write_argument_does_not_claim_an_uninit_buffer_was_filled.jet:5:10
    |
  5 |     noop(bytes)
    |          ^^^^^
 Why: `bytes` was declared with `Type{ uninit }`, so no value is available until you write to it — this read could see garbage
 Fix: Assign `bytes` on every path before reading it; a fixed list needs every slot assigned
More: jet-lang.dev/e/E0420
